part.text:
All 1936 symbol-solver tests pass.

## Fix

The issue was that `TypeExtractor` (which resolves expression types in the symbol solver) had no override for `TextBlockLiteralExpr`, so resolution fell through to `DefaultVisitorAdapter.visit(TextBlockLiteralExpr)` which throws `UnsupportedOperationException`.

Added a one-method fix in `javaparser-symbol-solver-core/src/main/java/com/github/javaparser/symbolsolver/javaparsermodel/TypeExtractor.java:293`:

```java
@Override
public ResolvedType visit(TextBlockLiteralExpr node, Boolean solveLambdas) {
    return stringReferenceType;
}
```

A text block is a `java.lang.String` literal, just like `StringLiteralExpr`, so it now resolves to the same String reference type. Verified with a reproduction of the issue's example — both `"...".formatted(...)` and the text-block variant now solve to `java.lang.String.formatted(java.lang.Object...)`.
